.offer-h{font-size:26px!important;}
}
</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#EADFCB;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;">
<span class="preheader">Three things people tell me before their first workshop. Half price through Monday.&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;</span>
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="background-color:#EADFCB;">
<tr><td align="center" style="padding:24px 12px;">
<table role="presentation" class="wrapper" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width:600px;background-color:#F4ECDF;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;">
<tr><td style="padding:0;"><a href="https://songdance.co/workshop?utm_source=broadcast&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=bfcm_2026&amp;utm_content=a-new2_hero&amp;{{prefill}}#register" style="display:block;"><img src="https://songdance.co/email/bfcm/A-2.jpg" width="600" alt="Black Friday: 50% off the workshop and the masterclass, through Monday 30 November" style="width:100%;height:auto;background-color:#4A3848;"></a></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:44px 44px 6px;"><p style="margin:0 0 22px;font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2.5px;color:#A14826;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;"><span style="display:inline-block;width:26px;height:1px;background-color:#A14826;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:12px;"></span>The workshop &amp; the masterclass</p><h1 class="h1" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:42px;line-height:1.12;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 28px;">Three things people tell me <em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">before the first time.</em></h1><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">Hello {{ subscriber.first_name | default: "there" }},</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;"><strong style="font-weight:600;">&ldquo;I can&rsquo;t sing.&rdquo;</strong> Good. This isn&rsquo;t singing. We say tone, never note. Trained singers sometimes have the harder start.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;"><strong style="font-weight:600;">&ldquo;Someone will hear me.&rdquo;</strong> Your microphone stays off unless you want it on. And soft counts. Soft often counts double.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;"><strong style="font-weight:600;">&ldquo;What if nothing comes?&rdquo;</strong> Then that is what&rsquo;s there. A closed door has a sound too, and we start with that one.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 0px;">Nothing here needs you to be ready. The workshop and the masterclass are half price through Monday 30&nbsp;November.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:34px 44px 6px;"><h2 class="offer-h" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.22;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 18px;">The questions, <em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">answered plainly</em></h2><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-bottom:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">&ldquo;Do I need to be able to sing?&rdquo;</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">No. You don&rsquo;t need a good voice, you need your honest one. You cannot do it wrong; it will always express something.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">&ldquo;Will I have to scream?&rdquo;</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">No. We don&rsquo;t go to screaming. One tone, the tone of what&rsquo;s there. That&rsquo;s the whole instruction.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">&ldquo;What about the neighbours?&rdquo;</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">The most common question in this work. Soft counts, and soft often counts double. A hum is a complete practice. Some people start in their car or their bathroom. Your microphone stays off unless you want it on.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">&ldquo;Is this a sound bath?&rdquo;</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">No. In a sound bath someone makes sound for you. Here you are the one sounding. Nobody does it to you, because nobody can.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">&ldquo;Is it safe if I&rsquo;m holding a lot of pain?&rdquo;</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">The voice will never force you. In our experience it seldom brings up more than you can be with. Seldom is not never, which is why volume is yours to set and stopping is always allowed. And this doesn&rsquo;t replace therapy. It was never intended to.</p></td></tr></table></td></tr>
