<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#EADFCB;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;">
<span class="preheader">Two ways back into the live sessions. Two days left.&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;</span>
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="background-color:#EADFCB;">
<tr><td align="center" style="padding:24px 12px;">
<table role="presentation" class="wrapper" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width:600px;background-color:#F4ECDF;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;">
<tr><td style="padding:0;"><a href="https://songdance.co/courses/certification?utm_source=broadcast&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=bfcm_2026&amp;utm_content=c-12w-ended2_hero&amp;{{prefill}}#register" style="display:block;"><img src="https://songdance.co/email/bfcm/C-2.jpg" width="600" alt="Black Friday: 50% off the certification course, 20% off live passes, through Monday 30 November" style="width:100%;height:auto;background-color:#4A3848;"></a></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:44px 44px 6px;"><p style="margin:0 0 22px;font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2.5px;color:#A14826;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;"><span style="display:inline-block;width:26px;height:1px;background-color:#A14826;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:12px;"></span>For those who did the 12 weeks</p><h1 class="h1" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:42px;line-height:1.12;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 28px;">You don&rsquo;t have to <em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">do it alone.</em></h1><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">Hello {{ subscriber.first_name | default: "there" }},</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">A practice kept alone tends to go quiet. Not because anything went wrong. Life is loud, and there is nobody to ask &ldquo;what is below that?&rdquo; when you would rather not look.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">In a Q&amp;A somebody else asks the question you didn&rsquo;t know you had. In a deepening session we take two hours for one theme. That is what the live sessions are for.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 0px;"><strong style="font-weight:600;">If you want them back:</strong> a live pass, 20% off. <strong style="font-weight:600;">If you have been wondering whether you could hold space for others:</strong> the certification course, half price. Both through Monday 30&nbsp;November.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:34px 44px 6px;"><h2 class="offer-h" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.22;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 18px;">What the live sessions <em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">are</em></h2><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-bottom:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">The weekly Q&amp;A</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">A live hour. This is where the smaller, in-between questions are met, where you bring what came up in a practice and we look at it together. Each replay stays available for two months.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">The monthly deepening session</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Two hours on one theme, with the wider community of practitioners.</p></td></tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:34px 44px 6px;"><h2 class="offer-h" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.22;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 18px;">What you learn in the <em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">certification course</em></h2><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">Your 12 weeks were for your own practice. These nine months are about sitting with someone else while they sound:</p><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-bottom:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">To travel through the layers of a sound</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">How to recognise feelings in a voice (high, low, trembling, sharp), how to follow what is underneath the first sound, and how to guide a whole session from beginning to end.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">The emotions underneath</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Anger, fear, pain and grief. How each one moves, how it disguises itself, and how to meet it through the voice.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">Listening with the body</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Telling grief from pain, fear from overwhelm. Hearing what the voice is almost saying.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">Skills for holding the space</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Pacing. Regulation. The volume button. Knowing when to lead, when to hold, and when to let the silence do the work.</p></td></tr></table><div style="height:18px;line-height:18px;font-size:0;">&nbsp;</div><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 0px;">A note on what it is not: it is not a comprehensive training to become a therapist, coach or psychologist. It is a course in Somatic Vocal Healing specifically. If you mean to work with clients professionally, you should already have a background in holding space.</p></td></tr>
